{"availability":"available","full":"RawLabs/MakerSim","name":"MakerSim","description":"Local CLI and MCP tools for experimental load-path analysis of 3D-printed STL parts, CAD revision comparisons, visual reviews, and human-guided engineering sessions.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-06T07:40:43Z","updated":"2026-10-11T01:40:12Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["3d-printing","cad","engineering","finite-element-analysis","mcp","mcp-server","model-context-protocol","python","simulation"],"demo":"https://makersim.rawcastdigital.com/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:58.169Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:58.169Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:58.169Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T06:14:58.169Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Live demo · Open the playground · Request a testing session","MakerSim helps makers explore how a force travels through a 3D-printed part. Upload an STL, choose your filament and print settings, paint the surfaces held still, and place a pull. An elasticity solver returns a relative stress heatmap and an optional movement preview with an adjustable display scale.","The landing page stays available when the testing server is offline. Its 3D hero uses a precomputed result from the included bracket; the playground runs your own simulation when the server is online. You can also run MakerSim locally."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RawLabs/MakerSim/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"371d65e7b2e3610a84fa65575580fd3bec850f2c306023ed30f131e8fca2be26","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:58.302Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:58.302Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Live demo · Open the playground · Request a testing session","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RawLabs/MakerSim/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirem